# Swellread environment
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT: nothing here is required. With no variables set the app uses
# an embedded PGlite database at ./.data/pglite and seeds its break catalogue on
# first run. `npm run dev` and `npm test` both work with zero configuration.
#
# PRODUCTION: the only variable that matters is DATABASE_URL, pointing at a hosted
# Postgres (Neon, Vercel Postgres, Supabase, anything that speaks the postgres://
# protocol). Without it the app refuses to start in production rather than silently
# accepting writes that vanish on the next cold start.

# Hosted Postgres connection string. Required in production.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/db?sslmode=require

# Deliberately allow the embedded store in production. Do not set this unless you
# understand that data will not survive a redeploy. Useful for preview deploys.
# SWELLREAD_ALLOW_LOCAL_STORE=1

# Absolute URL of the deployment, used for canonical tags, OpenGraph images and the
# sitemap. Set automatically by Vercel; override only if needed.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://swellread.vercel.app